Z||000000||next level trends prez||12-19-2001||09:50 PM||||my hydraulic clutch line went bad from a friend who broke it i got a new one i pulled the slave cylinder out then put it back in and then put the new line in.. now as much as i beed out the clutch it still is spungy and the clutch wont engage.. i had no probablems before the line was replaced... is there a trick to getting more pressure or what cause it just seems it needs more pressure to move it a little further...can anybody help.. my car runs great other than this...||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowCG||12-19-2001||10:08 PM||||My advice would be to replace both the master cyl.,and the slave cyl.,one first,in case you get lucky.<BR>Before that,you can check the action at the clutch rod;you should be able to get right around an inch of movement at the clutch rod,any less than 7/8",and you'll be grinding gears.<BR>Good luck.||||reg||1
